# Code generated by Claude
"""Search for a home pose ("zombie pose") that meets all the staging requirements with the most margin (David 2026-10-19). Report only: nothing in the config is changed.

    source .venv/bin/activate
    MUJOCO_GL=egl python experiments/home_pose_search.py --search [--minutes 40] [--out data/home_pose_search]
    MUJOCO_GL=egl python experiments/home_pose_search.py --report [--top 3]        # all margins, eagle and wrist camera images of the best distinct poses
    MUJOCO_GL=egl python experiments/home_pose_search.py --finder [RANK]           # the stance finder rerun for the RANK-th best pose (default 1)
    (one MuJoCo process at a time; everything is written under data/home_pose_search/, every evaluation is appended to evals.jsonl, so an interrupted search keeps what it found)

A pose is the left arm's 7 joints in degrees; the right arm is the mirror image (qR = (-q1, -q2, -q3, q4, -q5, -q6, -q7)). The scene, the stance and the checks are those of
experiments/home_pose_candidates.py: the open bench, the beaker and the hotplate where they are, the current staging stance's x, y and heading, the pedestal height free (0.06 to 0.22 m).

Hard conditions on the pose (a pose that breaks one scores below zero and is not evaluated further; "violation" says by how much): the grippers face forward (the approach axis within 10 deg
of horizontal and 15 deg of the heading, the finger-closing axis within 8 deg of horizontal), the tool point at about chest height (4 to 17 cm below the shoulder), forward of the torso (at
least 20 cm) and spread toward the sides (at least 15 cm from the centre line, the current pose's 15.3).

Requirements, each as a margin that is positive when it is met, in units of the requirement's own limit (1.0 is one limit's worth of slack):
    framing      (slack - 10 %) / 10 %: the largest worst-case margin any neck pose can give for the beaker's and hotplate's corners and both grippers (tool point, hand, finger tips); 10 % required
    occlusion    the share of the beaker's and the hotplate's pixels in the eagle camera's image (neck at its framing pose) that the robot hides (src/stance_checks.OcclusionMeter, David
                 2026-10-19; replaces the 18-point ray test). Two margins: the beaker may hide 0 %: -hidden share / 5 % when any is hidden, CAP when none is; the hotplate may hide 20 %:
                 (20 % - hidden share) / 20 %
    clearance    (distance - minimum) / minimum of every moving arm part to: the bench, the hotplate and the beaker where it stands (40 mm), the torso (30), pedestal (30), base (30), neck (40),
                 battery (40) and the other arm (40) (home_pose_test's minimums); the fingers alone to the bench and the hotplate (40); every arm part to a beaker placed on the hotplate (40)
    joint        (smallest distance of any joint of the pose to its limit, degrees - 10) / 10
    neck         (0.06 - spread) / 0.06: the neck framing's repeatability under 0.1 degree of arm noise
The score of a pose is the smallest of all these margins at its best pedestal height; the search maximizes its key: the smallest margin up to SCORE_CAP (0.3), plus 2 % of the mean margin (a tie-break, so that
it has a direction when the smallest margin is stuck), minus COVERAGE_WEIGHT times the arm coverage of the eagle image (the share of its pixels the arms cover, David 2026-10-20: once every margin is
comfortable the search prefers the pose whose arms cover less of the image) (a simple evolution strategy: samples around the mean of the best poses of the
generation, step sizes shrinking; four runs of a quarter of the time each, from pose C of experiments/home_pose_candidates.py, from pose B, from a C with the forearms turned out, and from the
best pose found so far). The stance's offset from the current staging stance (+-6 cm in x and y) is part of what is searched, since it moves the hand relative to the beaker's and the hotplate's line of sight.
"""

